  bootwright
      Coordinate declarative day-0 platform bootstrap

  Usage
    bootwright [command] [flags]

  Run the lifecycle
  COMMAND   PURPOSE
  plan      Preview an apply or a destroy without executing it
  apply     Apply the complete selected lifecycle unit
  destroy   Destroy the complete selected lifecycle unit

  Inspect and troubleshoot
  COMMAND   PURPOSE
  status    Show recorded lifecycle progress and next steps
  logs      Show a context's operation events and retained adapter output
  diff      Compare desired state with what this context realized
  explain   Explain the stop codes apply and destroy report
  check     Check input, this controller or an environment's prerequisites

  Prepare Bootwright and its inputs
  COMMAND      PURPOSE
  controller   Install, rebind or remove this host's controller
  catalog      Browse installer media, built-in add-ons and the desired-state schema
  context      Create, select, update and delete contexts
  secret       Set, generate, check and reveal a context's Secrets
  render       Render effective desired state and external-tool artifacts

  Work with machines and clusters
  COMMAND   PURPOSE
  machine   Inspect, reach, trust and power a context's Machines
  cluster   Inspect and reach a context's clusters

  CLI tools
  COMMAND      PURPOSE
  version      Show executable and dependency build identities
  sbom         Export this executable's software bill of materials
  completion   Generate shell completion scripts
  help         Show help for an exact command path

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  More detail
    Use --help --detail full to include SSH overrides.

  Examples
    bootwright check input --file ./input
    bootwright plan apply --context lab
    bootwright status --context lab
